The Reference grays are based on the matching 
of Multigrade FB IV.ppc, curve 3, and TMY 76+1.pfc, curve 8min sample files with matching ES values. These reference grays are scaled for other Matches, including the Zone V range (it is NOT fixed at 0.6 to 0.9 like previous versions of Matcher).
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 Matche
r documents store reference to film and paper files. If the film and/or paper file moves folders the matcher document will fail to reload.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
Along with the film and paper file references, the selected curves and a reference curve is saved in the Matcher d
ocument. Any analysis value changes are also saved in the Matcher document and will override the Film and Paper file values.  You can reload the original Film and Paper file values with an option on the Edit menu, Restore File Defaults.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
If the original Film and/or Paper file is updated and you have saved analysis overrides in the Matcher file, you will be asked if you wish to reload the analysis values from the original file.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
You can load a user defined reference curve in place of the default one.  On
 the curve menu, select Load Reference Curve and select a saved Matcher document.  This will load that Matcher curve as the new reference curve and allow you to directly compare new matches to your favorite matches. The selected Matcher document must have
 a valid match saved in order to load (i.e. both a film and paper curve were selected when the document was saved). The selection of the new reference curve is NOT saved in the Matcher document.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
The Simulate curve option is not functional
 but you can play with the dialog.  It will allow the creation of simulation curves as necessary. Once created, these will show in the film's curve list and will be available for selection just like normal film curves.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
There's an option to lock the Film's DR value to the selected Paper's ES value.  There is a checkbox on the Paper tab to activate this feature. If the box is left unchecked then the Film's ES value will always be the value entered on the Film tab.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl12\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\ilvl12\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
