\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid15686259 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid11218955 {\fs20\insrsid15686259 
Added the ability to export film test data to ExpoDev for PocketPC (currently in limited beta). This is accessed from the File menu while a film file is open. When exporting film data you have to provide the display name used in ExpoDev and the reciprocit
y
 curve model to use. Select a model that closely matches your film type.  If you are unsure, select the default model. Note that the ES value used in the analysis of the film data is also exported for use in ExpoDev and will automatically be set.  If you 
have several different ES values that you use you should export data for each combination.
